    "result": "Both routes retain stale immutable class output on the immediate changed-build request, then correct retry and settled results. Both cases remain incorrect and retain nonzero shutdown exits.",
    "boundary": "Class bytes are copied in a separately recorded post-response read interval and executed from that immutable copy. RPC reply time does not establish output freshness.",
    "recovery": "Repeated build requests can advance compilation; this is probe-driven recovery.",
    "interruption": "The earlier run has no original seal or final source-drift observation and its second report is unfinalized. Its raw subset is retained without reconstructing terminal events.",
    "artifactAudit": "The extracted review has no semantic integrity issues; a changed copied class is rejected. The original complete inventory is independently verified during packaging."
